 {id:'temp2020',type:'Peer-reviewed research',year:2020,title:'Brew temperature, at fixed brew strength and extraction, has little impact on the sensory profile of drip brew coffee',summary:'Drip brews at 87, 90, and 93°C showed little sensory difference when total dissolved solids and extraction yield were matched by adjusting other variables.',limit:'Controlled experimental design; this does not mean manual V60 temperature changes cannot affect extraction.',url:'https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-73341-4'},
 {id:'sensory2023',type:'Peer-reviewed research',year:2023,title:'A new Coffee Brewing Control Chart relating sensory properties and consumer liking to brew strength, extraction yield, and brew ratio',summary:'Measured strength, extraction and consumer preference do not map to one universal ideal; distinct taste preference clusters were identified.',limit:'Studied drip-brewed coffee; not a validated grind or temperature recipe for any individual origin.',url:'https://doi.org/10.1111/1750-3841.16531'},
 {id:'roast2020',type:'Peer-reviewed research',year:2020,title:'Effects of brew strength, brew yield, and roast on the sensory quality of drip brewed coffee',summary:'Sensory perception varied systematically with strength, extraction yield and roast level across controlled drip brews.',limit:'Does not supply an exact best hand-pour schedule for every roast.',url:'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32652586/'},
 {id:'processing2023',type:'Scientific review',year:2023,title:'Coffee bean processing: Emerging methods and their effects on chemical, biological and sensory properties',summary:'Fermentation and emerging processing methods can change aroma precursors and sensory properties, with outcomes dependent on conditions.',limit:'Do not infer the meaning of a producer-specific label such as “melon-washed” without the roaster’s description.',url:'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030881462300105X'},
 {id:'aroma2023',type:'Scientific review',year:2023,title:'Effects of postharvest processing on aroma formation in roasted coffee – a review',summary:'Dry/natural, honey, washed and roast processes can affect volatile compounds associated with aroma.',limit:'Describes mechanisms and trends, not a guaranteed flavor note for each processing method.',url:'https://doi.org/10.1111/ijfs.16261'},
 {id:'terroir2022',type:'Peer-reviewed review',year:2022,title:'Does Coffee Have Terroir and How Should It Be Assessed?',summary:'Environment, cultivar, postharvest processing, roast, grind and brew together influence the sensory expression of origin.',limit:'Country borders are poor predictors of a unique scientifically optimal brewing setting.',url:'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35804722/'},
 {id:'fermentation2025',type:'Systematic review & meta-analysis',year:2025,title:'Unraveling the impact of coffee fermentation: Interactions among processing variables and their effects on sensory quality',summary:'Across 22 studies, fermentation effects depended on approach, oxygen environment, duration and method; protocols vary.',limit:'Sensory outcomes are heterogeneous. This is not proof anaerobic coffees must be brewed cooler.',url:'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tifs.2025.105151'},
 {id:'sca',type:'Industry reference',year:2019,title:'Specialty Coffee Association Coffee Brewing Control Chart',summary:'Historically used filter-coffee reference area: approximately 18–22% extraction yield and 1.15–1.35% beverage TDS.',limit:'The conventional chart is a reference region, not a universal preference rule. You cannot measure extraction yield from time and ratio alone.',url:'https://static1.squarespace.com/static/587af1d4db29d69a1a226b95/t/60aece65e4f2134d99f6e646/1622068839009/SCA%2BBrewing%2BChart%2B-%2BRevised%2BMarch%2B2019-US-Letter.pdf'},
 {id:'grinder',type:'Manufacturer specification',year:2023,title:'1Zpresso X-Ultra official manual and adjustment chart',summary:'X-Ultra has 4.5 total rotations; 60 clicks per full rotation, 10 clicks between numbered positions, and nominal burr movement of 12.5µm per click.',limit:'Burr movement per click is not the same thing as ground-particle diameter. Record settings from your own zero point.',url:'https://1zpresso.coffee/jp/manual-xultra-en/'},
 {id:'hario',type:'Manufacturer specification',year:2025,title:'Hario V60 Dripper NEO 02',summary:'Hario describes 72 ribs converging to 9; size 02 accommodates about 1–4 cups. Flow may differ from a conventional V60.',limit:'Manufacturer flavor claims are not controlled evidence of an ideal drawdown time.',url:'https://hario-asia-official.com/products/hario-v60-dripper-neo'}
